{"_type":"issue","id":"samples-20260717-jl2","title":"samples-20260717 workspace bootstrap","description":"# Wayfinder Map — samples-20260717 workspace bootstrap\n\n## Destination\n\nA fully wired project workspace on `samples-20260717` where: **bd** holds tasks/issues, **Infisical** holds secrets (single source of truth), **SAGE** holds governed agent memory (`project/samples-20260717`), **Siyuan** holds project PKM (full integration), **AGENTS.md** routes to global `~/.config/agents/AGENTS.md`, and **~/docs/** records the integration (full parity). All scoped per-host via direnv, fail-closed, mirroring the chinook-laravel pattern where one exists.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Skills every session consults:** `sage-home`, `sage-usage`, `beads`, `wayfinder`.\n- **Reference impl:** `~/Herd/chinook-laravel` for beads/SAGE/AGENTS.md; **none** for Siyuan (first-of-kind → research ticket).\n- **Tracker:** bd (beads) — overrides the global GitHub Issues default for this repo.\n- **Standing preferences:** Infisical as source of truth, `.env.sage` as cache; 1 shared SAGE token; all 7 hosts; fail-closed on missing identity.\n- **Playbooks:** `docs/20-operations/2005-memory/200502-project-integration-guide.md` (generic), `200517-chinook-laravel-integration-example.md` (worked example).\n\n## Decisions so far\n\n- Namespace `project/samples-20260717` (matches repo dir).\n- SAGE token model: **1 shared bearer** across all hosts (single-operator trade-off: lose per-host revocation, gain one secret).\n- Secret store: **Infisical** (not hand-written `.env.sage`); `.env.sage` is hydrated cache + offline fallback.\n- Hosts: **all 7** — OpenCode, Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Zed, Junie, GitHub Copilot.\n- Env-var layering: 4 export names cover 7 hosts — `SAGE_OPENCODE_*`, `SAGE_CODEX_*`, `SAGE_CLAUDE_*`, unprefixed `SAGE_MCP_*` (Cursor/Zed/Junie/Copilot).\n- Siyuan: full integration; research ticket decides the how.\n- docs: full parity (index registration + worked-example + project `docs/agents/`).\n\n## Not yet specified\n\n- Siyuan isolation/token model (per-notebook token vs global token + ACL) — graduates after the Siyuan research ticket.\n- Siyuan agent access path (MCP server vs direct HTTP) — graduates after the Siyuan research ticket.\n- Beads Dolt sync behaviour over the GitHub remote — resolves during the beads bootstrap ticket.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- `sage-pgaak` server project-scoping (separate identity/persona).\n- Spoke Worker Memory / Hub \u0026 Spoke registration.\n- Editing any host's **global** config (`~/.opencode/opencode.json`, `~/.codex/config.toml`, `~/.claude.json`, `~/.cursor/mcp.json`).\n- Storing task state in SAGE (bd owns that).\n- Infisical workspace-level secret changes (project-scoped only).\n- Tier-2 hosts whose HTTP-MCP support is unconfirmed — document + revert if unsupported.\n","notes":"DECISION (jl2.5 Siyuan research, closed): global API token model; HTTP access; notebook 20260719071714-xyhlut0. Open fork for jl2.6: discipline-vs-second-container isolation.\nDECISION (jl2.1 Beads, closed): bd init auto-configured correctly. no-git-ops=true retained (conservative); user pushes Dolt sync explicitly.\nDECISION (jl2.10 substrate, closed): agent_key_file was empty in data/config.yaml; fixed to /root/.sage/agent.key. DECISION (jl2.3 SAGE, closed): namespace + token done; v11 node-operator auth model confirmed (domain-tag scoping, not per-project agent identity).\nDECISION (jl2.4 direnv, closed): .envrc + whitelist + verify done; 4-host-name export pattern proven.\nDECISION (jl2.7 hosts, closed): 4 project configs authored. .zed + .vscode are gitignored by existing repo stance (local-only); .mcp.json + .cursor/mcp.json tracked. Canonical URL /v1/mcp (no port).\nDECISION (jl2.6 Siyuan, closed): discipline-based isolation chosen. Notebook created, global token wired, HTTP access verified. No MCP (direct API). Risk: global-admin token; AGENTS.md guardrail required.\nDECISION (jl2.8 AGENTS.md, closed): header prepended; global